XR diorama and window: see Link through what stands in front of him, and the window's clip plane

GX_AURORA_SET_SEE_THROUGH (AuroraSetSeeThrough): a point in the head's space (Link, from the game) and
a cone from the eyes' midpoint toward it. The draws the view delta applies to (the world's) carry it in
their uniform, and their fragments within the cone and nearer than the point by more than a margin are
discarded, dithered over a soft edge, so what stands between the eyes and Link (trees, grass, walls) is
cut away and Link and what is behind him show. The same cut for both eyes (a volume in the head's
space), so the hole is solid in 3D. The margin keeps Link's own draws (and the ground at his feet); the
HUD and the 2D are not the world's draws.

GX_AURORA_SET_CLIP_PLANE (AuroraSetClipPlane): a plane in the head's space; the world's fragments on
its positive side are discarded. The window (mode = ventana) puts it at the front of what may come out
of it, so what the game camera sees nearer is not drawn and what is behind it shows (instead of the
eyes' mask fading it into a see-through hole).

Both off at the end of each frame. The world's shaders take the view-space position as one more
varying, and every GX shader carries the discards (a uniform branch); the uniforms are 48 bytes longer
(MaxUniformSize with them).

